@title PCSA00015 campaign race - boot to a LIVE RACE on the campaign's first event
@game  PCSA00015

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
#   boot -> PRESS ANY BUTTON -> GAME MODE -> SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN
#        -> campaign intro -> the campaign MAP -> select the event EMPIRE CLIMB
#        -> event briefing -> confirm -> SHIP SELECT -> the race is LIVE.
#
# At the end of this recipe the title is racing: the world pass carries several
# hundred draws and tens of thousands of triangles, `camera` tracks the ship,
# and holding `r` (thrust) flies it down the track.
#
# >>> IT NEEDS `VITASLOP_FRAME_TOPUP=0`, AND THAT IS NOT OPTIONAL.
# With the default per-flip clock top-up a displayed frame carries about a
# TENTH of the guest work a console frame carries, and this title never
# finishes loading at all. See `VitaState::advance_time_frame`.
#
#   VITASLOP_FRAME_TOPUP=0 play --game <dir> --recipe <this> --max-frames 50000
#
# >>> WHY THE MAP SECTION IS A SWEEP OF 35 TAPS AND NOT ONE TAP
# The campaign map is a PANNABLE hex grid, and it is drawn by a shader that
# builds its vertices from a texture fetch - so no fixed-function renderer can
# show it and there is no picture to read a node's position off. The sweep is
# how the node was found: it pans the map and taps across it, and the tap at
# f39800 lands on an event node. That is measured, not guessed - the title
# spawns its LoadingScreenThread three frames later
# (`RUST_LOG=vitaslop::thread=debug`), which is the signal this whole sequence
# was tuned against. Every tap before it is load-bearing: they set the pan the
# last tap depends on. Do not "tidy" them away.
#
# >>> THE GESTURE TYPE MASK MATTERS AND THE DEFAULT IS NOW RIGHT
# SceSystemGesture recognizers come in types 1/2/4/8 and their meanings are not
# published. Reporting a touch to ALL of them tells the title a tap and a drag
# and a pinch happened at once, and the map then only ever PANS - no tap sweep
# selects anything. Type 1 alone selects. `vita::gesture::type_mask` now
# defaults to 1 for that reason; `VITASLOP_GESTURE_TYPE_MASK=15` reproduces the
# old behaviour and this recipe then reaches the map and stops there.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
# No input while it loads - this is boot.recipe's ladder, unchanged.

28000: cross
28000: @shot title-screen
28020:
# "PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START" -> GAME MODE.

28620: touch=472,524
28620: @shot game-mode
28640:
# The SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN tile (screen 236,262). ONLINE CAMPAIGN and
# CROSS-PLAY are correctly greyed out (signed out); ADHOC needs a second unit.

29040: cross
29040: @shot campaign-intro
29060:
# The intro text ("Touch the nodes to play events").

29460: touch=1760,952
29460: @shot campaign-intro-confirm
29480:
# Its confirm checkmark, bottom right (screen 880,476).

33000: @section campaign-map
33000: @shot campaign-map
# The map renders only its HUD - see the header for why. The sweep follows.
33000: touch=250,250
33015:
33200: touch=500,250
33215:
33400: touch=750,250
33415:
33600: touch=1000,250
33615:
33800: touch=1250,250
33815:
34000: touch=1500,250
34015:
34200: touch=1700,250
34215:
34400: touch=250,400
34415:
34600: touch=500,400
34615:
34800: touch=750,400
34815:
35000: touch=1000,400
35015:
35200: touch=1250,400
35215:
35400: touch=1500,400
35415:
35600: touch=1700,400
35615:
35800: touch=250,550
35815:
36000: touch=500,550
36015:
36200: touch=750,550
36215:
36400: touch=1000,550
36415:
36600: touch=1250,550
36615:
36800: touch=1500,550
36815:
37000: touch=1700,550
37015:
37200: touch=250,700
37215:
37400: touch=500,700
37415:
37600: touch=750,700
37615:
37800: touch=1000,700
37815:
38000: touch=1250,700
38015:
38200: touch=1500,700
38215:
38400: touch=1700,700
38415:
38600: touch=250,850
38615:
38800: touch=500,850
38815:
39000: touch=750,850
39015:
39200: touch=1000,850
39215:
39400: touch=1250,850
39415:
39600: touch=1500,850
39615:
39800: touch=1700,850
39815:

# The tap above at f39800 (touch=1700,850) is the one that lands on an event
# node: EMPIRE CLIMB, a RACE with NO WEAPONS. The title starts loading it three
# frames later.

40000: @section event-loading
40000: @shot event-loading
# The loading screen carries the title's own control legend, which is where the
# race controls below come from: STEER/PITCH = LEFT STICK, R = THRUST,
# X = FIRE/USE PICKUP, plus airbrake and absorb.

43600: @shot event-briefing
# EMPIRE CLIMB / RACE, with a confirm checkmark bottom right.

44000: @section confirm-event
44000: touch=1760,960
44020:
44400: @shot after-confirm

44600: @section race
# From here the title is in the event: `start` opens the in-race GAME PAUSED
# menu (OPTIONS / PHOTO MODE, and quit / restart / resume buttons), and the
# frame is a race frame - a 1024x1024 shadow pass, reflection and post targets,
# and a world pass of several hundred draws into an offscreen 960x544 target
# that the composite samples.
#
# @note The composite CANNOT be reproduced by the software renderer: its
# fullscreen blit carries no texcoord attribute (the shader derives the UV), so
# `@shot` here is the HUD over black. The race itself is fine - render the
# world pass with VITASLOP_SW_CHAIN=1 VITASLOP_SW_CHAIN_DIR=<dir> and look at
# pass05_89204aa0.png, which shows the ship on the track.
#
# @todo Drive it. `camera` gives the ship's position and heading every frame and
# `surface --tex <track>` gives how far the track material reaches ahead, which
# together close a steering loop (a controller that does this holds ~80 world
# units per 30 frames along the track). What is NOT solved is finishing: the
# ship still scrapes walls and is destroyed and respawned, and no lap or
# progress value has been located yet. There is no @assert here for that reason.
50000: @section end
